{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788384345,"nonce":"X8c6AGE4JrpypDAxihHDCK5WTnY=","title":"Found in play, run openrun-20260902, day 5 Summer (tick ~501,000). Dorian","message":"resolved it by hand; the agent had no route to it.\n\n\nQuest \"The Solitary Knight\" (accepted, Ongoing). The lodger Eurplaerepla is\n`faction: PlayerColony`, `class: colonist`, standing 16 cells from his own\nshuttle (`Shuttle` id 13252 at [88,101]). The shuttle had arrived 13,500+ ticks\nearlier and he would not board — job stayed `wandering.` while the quest sat\nOngoing with every `QuestPart_Delay` and `QuestPart_ShuttleDelay` already\n`Disabled`/`ticks_left: 0`.\n\n**The human fix was to flick AUTOLOAD on the shuttle.** That is a gizmo toggle\non the building. Nothing in the verb surface can reach it.\n\n\n    orders {pawn:13246, cell:\"88,101\"}   -\u003e available 0, blocked 0\n    orders {pawn:13246, thing:13252}     -\u003e available 0, blocked 0\n    prioritize {pawn, work:\"GrowerHarvest\"} (earlier, same family)\n      -\u003e \"no WorkGiverDef named ...\" / \"the game offers no option for this\n          work giver on this target (not directOrderable, not a\n          WorkGiver_Scanner, ...). Call `orders` for what IS offered.\"\n\nSo `orders` — the verb the refusal points you at — reports **nothing at all**,\nneither available nor blocked, for a target that demonstrably has a player\naction on it. It is not wrong: entering a transporter is not a WorkGiver, and\n`orders` is a work-giver probe. It is simply blind to this whole class.\n\n\n`flick` exists and covers `CompFlickable` (power switches, lamps). It does not\ncover **`Command_Toggle` gizmos**, which is where a large amount of ordinary\nplay lives:\n\n- shuttle / transporter **autoload**  (this issue)\n- turret **hold fire**\n- door **hold open**\n- vent and cooler direction flip\n- trap / IED **arm-disarm**\n- animal **allow milking / shearing / slaughter** toggles\n- storage **priority** and the bill-giver toggles that are not bill fields\n\nNone of these is a WorkGiver, so `orders` cannot see them; none is a\n`CompFlickable`, so `flick` cannot touch them. They are `Gizmo`s returned by\n`Thing.GetGizmos()`, and the verb surface has no reader and no writer for that\nlist at all.\n\n\nThis one nearly cost a quest reward and there was no in-protocol recovery — the\nrun would have had to escalate to the human, which for an unattended agent is\nthe failure mode the whole surface exists to avoid. More generally, \"read the\nbuttons this thing offers, then press one\" is how a human plays RimWorld, and\nit is the one interaction channel the mod does not model. `orders` models the\nright-click menu; there is no equivalent for the selected-thing gizmo bar.\n\n\n- A read verb enumerates a thing's gizmos: for each, its label, its type\n  (`Command_Toggle` / `Command_Action` / `Command_SetTargetFuelLevel` ...), its\n  current state where it is a toggle, and whether it is currently disabled with\n  the game's own `disabledReason`.\n- A write verb invokes one by a stable identifier, reproducing the widget gate\n  rather than calling the underlying field — same discipline as every other\n  player verb (DESIGN §Action model), and refusing with `disabledReason` when\n  the game would have drawn it greyed out.\n- Round-trip acceptance: toggle autoload on a shuttle, read it back as on,\n  toggle it off, read it back as off.\n- `orders`, when it finds nothing, says whether the target has gizmos that this\n  other verb would expose — so the \"call `orders`\" advice in `prioritize`'s\n  refusal does not dead-end the caller the way it did here.\n- Out of scope, deliberately: `dev:*` shortcuts. The point is to reproduce what\n  a player can press, not to bypass it.\n\nRelated: git-bug `36c03c9` (pickup/equip/drop engine) is the same shape one\nlayer down — a whole class of ordinary player action that the verb set cannot\ncompose. Worth deciding whether both are answered by one \"act on this thing\"\nsurface.","files":null}]}